# Neoguard OS (NetGuard) – Deep Dive

![Neoguard OS logo](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LGxNDaRY-GeekedOutAi/Neoguard-OS-Deep-Dive/main/assets/logo.png)

---

## 🎯 Project Purpose  

**NetGuard** (branded as **Neoguard OS**) is a Windows‑focused network‑security agent that runs from the system tray. Its primary goals are:

| Goal | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Real‑time monitoring** | Tracks every outbound/inbound connection, enriches IPs/processes (PTR/ASN/org/datacenter flags) and logs blocked/suspicious events. |
| **AI‑augmented verdicts** | Integrates with a local LM Studio server (OpenAI‑compatible) using the custom model `netguard-llm` to generate contextual alerts and RAG‑driven learning from past events. |
| **Headless diagnostics** | `python -m netguard --diagnostic N` produces an N‑second snapshot + firewall report for automated auditing or CI pipelines. |
| **Self‑protection** | Tamper‑guard safeguards the runtime files, SQLite database (`netguard.db`), and the `allow_exe` table from unauthorized modification. Optional Windows ACL lockdown (`icacls.exe`) can be enabled for extra hardening. |
| **Training & red‑team lab** | Continuous attack simulator (RFC 5737 IPs, dry‑run firewall) grades live LLM verdicts and feeds mistakes into an `ExperienceStore` for immediate RAG learning. |

---

## ✨ Feature‑Rich Implementations  

| Category | Highlights |
|----------|------------|
| **Core monitoring** | • Connection monitor <br>• Process/IP enrichment <br>• Audit log (`block_events`) |
| **Persistence** | SQLite `netguard.db` (WAL mode) – rules, IP intel, settings (`allow_dirs`, `autostart`, profile lockdown). All access goes through a lock‑guarded connection with busy timeout. |
| **AI Sentinel LLM** | Configurable base URL/model/context length via DB settings, env vars, or `.env`. Falls back to code defaults. Used for verdict generation and red‑team grading. |
| **Tamper guard** | Protects runtime files, SQLite config (`sentinel_mode`), `allow_exe` table. Optional `icacls.exe` lockdown for `netguard.db`, `experience.db`, launcher files. |
| **Training lab** | Generates realistic network/hardware‑abuse scenarios, grades sentinel verdicts, stores mistakes for immediate learning. |
| **Throughput & telemetry** | `python -m netguard.smoke_throughput` exercises real host counters; module `netguard.throughput`. |
| **Forensic exporter** | Unit tests & exporter for incident bundles (`netguard.incident`). |
| **Multi‑theme engine** | UI theme support with dedicated unit tests (`netguard.theme`). |
| **Launch & autostart** | Bat/PS scripts (`launch_netguard_sentinel.bat`, `start_netguard.ps1`) handle elevation, reboot persistence, and “Restart‑as‑Admin” flows. |
| **Package layout** | `netguard/__main__.py` as entry point; sub‑packages: `database`, `firewall_engine`, `sentinel_ai`, `tray`, `connection_monitor`, `hw_telemetry`, `lora_trainer`, `training_scheduler`, `theme`, etc. |

---

## 📦 Repository Structure (high‑level)
Neoguard-OS-Deep-Dive/ │ ├─ .gitignore ├─ README.md ← this file ├─ pyproject.toml ├─ package.json │ └─ netguard/ # main Python package ├─ init.py ├─ main.py # python -m netguard entry point ├─ database.py # SQLite wrapper, WAL mode ├─ firewall_engine.py # Rule engine & blocking logic ├─ sentinel_ai.py # LLM integration (netguard‑llm) ├─ tray.py # System‑tray UI (PySide6) ├─ connection_monitor.py # Real‑time network monitoring ├─ theme.py # Multi‑theme engine ├─ throughput.py # Throughput sampling & smoke test ├─ incident.py # Forensic exporter ├─ monitors/ # per‑monitor modules │ └─ net.py ├─ training_scheduler.py # LLM‑training schedule ├─ hw_telemetry.py # Hardware telemetry collector └─ ... (additional sub‑packages as needed)




